 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Over three hundred millimetres of rain. Now a Canadian village is on evacuation alert."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "A chain of Pacific storms has soaked southwest British Columbia since Tuesday. The CBC reports up to three hundred and six millimetres at Port Mellon, northwest of Vancouver. Environment Canada says two hundred and fourteen fell there in just twenty-four hours."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "In Pemberton, north of Whistler, officials warn of extremely high river flows. On Wednesday, homes on Airport Road were ordered out, and the whole village was put on evacuation alert. Near Squamish, residents were told to shelter in place as water rose."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "On Vancouver Island, The Canadian Press reports floodwater backing up into basements in Port Alberni. Close to half a million B.C. Hydro customers lost power during the storms. And Environment Canada warned of possible widespread flooding."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Pemberton's evacuation alert be lifted by the weekend? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
