  "title": "B.C. Floods Force Evacuations Near Whistler #shorts",
  "description": "A chain of Pacific storms has dropped up to 306 mm of rain on southwest British Columbia since Tuesday, according to the CBC – Environment Canada measured 214 mm in 24 hours at Port Mellon. Pemberton ordered homes on Airport Road evacuated and put the whole village on evacuation alert, while residents near Squamish were told to shelter in place.\n\nSources: CBC News, The Canadian Press (via CTV News), The Globe and Mail, Environment and Climate Change Canada, EmergencyInfoBC / Village of Pemberton (based on search-result excerpts). Rain areas on the map are illustrative and the river course is approximate.\n\n#climate #weather #bcflood #atmosphericriver #britishcolumbia",
